# Repo-root build-context excludes.
#
# Applies to every image built with `context: .` (the repo root): currently
# demo_api_server, demo_authz_server, and demo_mcp_gateway. Until this file
# existed there was NO .dockerignore for those builds (a service-local
# demo_api_server/.dockerignore is never consulted when the context is the repo
# root), so `COPY demo_api_server/ .` copied the host's stale node_modules OVER
# the clean `npm ci` install — making image contents depend on host state
# (e.g. zod pinned to whatever version happened to be on disk).
#
# Only list things that are NEVER build inputs. The repo-root Dockerfiles need
# demo_api_server/**, demo_authz_server/**, demo_mcp_gateway/**,
# oauth-mcp/openapi/**, demo_mcp_resource_server/openapi/**, scope-topology.json,
# service-topology.json, and docs/** — none of which are excluded here.

# Never copy host node_modules into an image; npm ci/npm install provides them.
**/node_modules

# VCS, agent worktrees, and editor scratch dirs — large and irrelevant to builds.
# (.claude holds nested git worktrees; sending it as context was very expensive.)
.git
.gitignore
.claude
.zed-worktrees

# Runtime logs, caches, OS cruft, and test artifacts.
**/*.log
**/logs
**/.DS_Store
**/coverage
**/.vite
**/.turbo
test-results

# Never bake live secrets into images (BFF now COPYs first-party trees into
# /repo for the SE/K8 default code-search indexer; Compose still bind-mounts
# ./:/repo over that path). Keep example envs.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/certs
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.crt
